" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=\\sqrt{5}$ and $b=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280585" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-280585" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280585" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280585" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280585" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-16552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\frac{3p+2q\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}}=1+2\\text{i}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-16552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2-3\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3p+2q\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}} & =1+2\\text{i} \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =(1+2\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i}) \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =2-3\\text{i}+4\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =2+\\text{i}-6(-1) \\\\ 3p+2q\\text{i} & =8+\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3p & =8 \\\\ p & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2q & =1 \\\\ q & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{8}{3}$ and $q=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-16552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-16552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-16552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=-3$, $q=2$"] ["text" "$p=-4$, $q=1$"] ["text" "$p=-\\frac{3}{4}$, $q=\\frac{3}{2}$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{4}{3}$, $q=-\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{8}{3}$, $q=\\frac{1}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-16552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=\\frac{8}{3}$, $q=\\frac{1}{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-275089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If  $6-\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{2+3\\text{i}},$ then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-275089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2+3\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-\\text{i}=\\frac{p+q\\text{i}}{2+3\\text{i}} \\\\ (6-\\text{i})(2+3\\text{i}) & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 12+18\\text{i}-2\\text{i}-3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 12+3+16\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ 15+16\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n15=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=15$ and $q=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-275089" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-275089" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-275089" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "15"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-275089" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-275089" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\frac{6+13\\text{i}}{5}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2-\\text{i}}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2-\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6+13\\text{i}}{5} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2-\\text{i}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(6+13\\text{i})(2-\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(12-6\\text{i}+26\\text{i}-13{\\text{i}}^{2}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(12+13+20\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}(25+20\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 5+4\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n5=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=5$ and $q=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8412" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-8412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=-4$, $q=-3$"] ["text" "$p=1$, $q=-\\,\\frac{3}{5}$"] ["text" "$p=5$, $q=4$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{1}{5}$, $q=-\\,\\frac{3}{5}$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{2}{5}$, $q=\\frac{4}{5}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8412" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=5$, $q=4$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $-3-2\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}}$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3-2\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}} \\\\ 2\\text{i}(-3-2\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 4-6\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n4=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-8408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=-4$, $q=-6$"] ["text" "$p=-6$, $q=-4$"] ["text" "$p=2$, $q=-3$"] ["text" "$p=4$, $q=-6$"] ["text" "$p=6$, $q=-4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=4$, $q=-6$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $-4+\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $2\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{2\\text{i}} \\\\ (-4+\\text{i})(2\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -8\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -2-8\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n-2=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-8 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-2$ and $q=-8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160043" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-160043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p=-1,q=-4"] ["math" "p=-1,q=4"] ["math" "p=-2,q=-8"] ["math" "p=-2,q=3"] ["math" "p=-4,q=2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p=-2,q=-8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $5-\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+2\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3+2\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5-\\text{i}}{3+2\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5-\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})}{(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{15-3\\text{i}-10\\text{i}+2{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{9+4} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13-13\\text{i}}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 1-\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=1$ and $q=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-8036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=-1$, $q=-1$"] ["text" "$p=-3$, $q=-3$"] ["text" "$p=1$, $q=-1$"] ["text" "$p=2$, $q=-3$"] ["text" "$p=\\frac{3}{2}$, $q=-\\frac{3}{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=1$, $q=-1$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $5=(p+q\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3+\\text{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =(p+q\\text{i})(3+\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{5}{3+\\text{i}} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(5)(3-\\text{i})}{(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{{3}^{2}-(\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{9+1} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{15-5\\text{i}}{10} & =p+q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i} & =p+q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{3}{2}=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-\\frac{1}{2}=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $q=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160049" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-160049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p=-\\frac{3}{2},q=\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "p=\\frac{2}{5},q=-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "p=\\frac{3}{5},q=-\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160049" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p=\\frac{3}{2},q=-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\frac{13\\text{i}}{2-3\\text{i}}=p+\\text{i}q,$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2-3\\text{i})(2+3\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{(2)^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{13\\text{i}(2+3\\text{i})}{13} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\text{i}(2+3\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 2\\text{i}+3{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -3+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-3=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $2=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-3$ and $q=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-8407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$p=-1$, $q=1$"] ["text" "$p=-3$, $q=2$"] ["text" "$p=-5$, $q=2$"] ["text" "$p=2$, $q=3$"] ["text" "$p=3$, $q=-4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-8407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=-3$, $q=2$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\frac{6-7\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}}=2p-5q\\text{i}$, then$\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}\nand\n$q=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-7\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{(6-7\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})}{(3-2\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18+12\\text{i}-21\\text{i}-14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18-9\\text{i}-14(-1)}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32-9\\text{i}}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32}{13}-\\frac{9}{13}\\text{i} & =2p-5q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{32}{13}=2p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-\\frac{9}{13}=-5q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{16}{13}$ and $q=\\frac{9}{65}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280406" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-280406" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280406" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{16}{13}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280406" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-280406" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{65}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $1+7\\text{i}=(p+\\text{i}q)(3-4\\text{i})$, calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $3-4\\text{i}$ to isolate the\n  variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+7\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(3-4\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{1+7\\text{i}}{3-4\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(1+7\\text{i})(3+4\\text{i})}{(3-4\\text{i})(3+4\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3+21\\text{i}+4\\text{i}+28{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{-25+25\\text{i}}{9+16} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{-25+25\\text{i}}{25} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ -1+\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $-1=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=-1$ and $q=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fe1e7b539130f0ecf369913c8a8630b81b9282ef6b03e61f98e980db6744834d"} {"question" "q-160050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p=-1,q=1"] ["math" "p=-1,q=2"] ["math" "p=-2,q=1"] ["math" "p=1,q=1"] ["math" "p=2,q=1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "q-160050" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p=-1,q=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/state.json" "file_sha256" "40664323ae02e1fdfb3495888fa2b9cdb85516cdc2fe4770d2ad5c977b7c6867"} {"question" "e-5245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $3+2\\textrm{i} = a + \\textrm{i}b,$ calculate the value of $a$ and the value of $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5245.json" "file_sha256" "0d07dd7758e08dcf6ad5312dae0216219010207c68790ce361384b63a7fc4494"} {"question" "e-5245" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we equate the real parts:\n\n$$\n3 = a\n$$\n\nThen, we equate the imaginary parts:\n\n$$\n2 = b\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3$ and $b=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5245.json" "file_sha256" "0d07dd7758e08dcf6ad5312dae0216219010207c68790ce361384b63a7fc4494"} {"question" "e-5261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $2 - 3 \\textrm{i} = \\dfrac{p - 2q \\textrm{i} }{1 + 2 \\textrm{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5261.json" "file_sha256" "e9ab835868a153395504f7236a75a77c7c12b382f412de0d9be0d17c97c1c4b6"} {"question" "e-5261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1+2\\textrm{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & =\\frac{p-2q\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ (2-3\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i}) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+4\\text{i}-3\\text{i}-6{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i}-6(-1) & =p-2q\\text{i} \\\\ 8+\\text{i} & =p-2q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8 = p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-2q \\\\ q & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5261.json" "file_sha256" "e9ab835868a153395504f7236a75a77c7c12b382f412de0d9be0d17c97c1c4b6"} {"question" "e-5293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $3+5\\textrm{i} = (p+\\textrm{i}q)(1+\\textrm{i}),$ calculate $p$ and $q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5293.json" "file_sha256" "9d747b6b200afde165ecf40afb6fc21c7d0734fb9467407ca5ef6e0ad72183fa"} {"question" "e-5293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both sides of the equation by $1+\\textrm{i}$ to isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & =(p+\\text{i}q)(1+\\text{i}) \\\\ \\frac{3+5\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(3+5\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})}{(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3-3\\text{i}+5\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{3+2\\text{i}-5(-1)}{1-(-1)} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ \\frac{8+2\\text{i}}{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 4+\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $4=p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $1=q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=4$ and $q=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/example-5293.json" "file_sha256" "9d747b6b200afde165ecf40afb6fc21c7d0734fb9467407ca5ef6e0ad72183fa"} {"question" "q-8407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$p=-3$, $q=2$"] "category" "reviewed_ma_solution" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041873/answer-source-reviews.json" "file_sha256" "f88cc9533e2c58ae1bfc2ac7b83ed9f7f16c8fafa6496a0a98f2a2a41d06dd88" "reviewer_session" "01a108cd-e7f4-73f3-b8fc-c82135bc6b7d" "rationale" "Multiplying numerator and denominator by 2+3i gives 13i(2+3i)/(4+9)=i(2+3i)=−3+2i. Equating real and imaginary parts yields p=−3 and q=2, original option e (index 4). The authentic worked solution and saved Correct grade agree. The stored p=3, q=−4 contradicts this calculation and must remain distinct." "bindings" {"problem" "f74b11668840c6f521b8d86a15c86181e6132b86e0c826a36a813d5f8188fc9d" "worked_solution" "c4d8dd65434800666d42f0d641182f931acb6dbd98ceb89424fee3c01caec8ff" "original_field" "fae908a86d3529138adebbd39668d80a12a14aa34aa4408c443e6bf450209f13" "reviewed_field" "6e8a3fca4d5fe4ea9ea3b86fe8e0d598cd3b475d272f6732a16dfc